+## Synthetic preflight scope
+
+On 2026-09-13 the integrator authorized parser-function qualification using
+small in-memory ZIPs and literal pickle byte strings only. The qualification
+must run as `static-preflight01` under `-I -S -B`, block the checkpoint open,
+and never call the reader's `main` or `inspect`. It checks successful stored
+and deflated containers and strict refusals for ambiguous/missing pickle
+members, unsafe or overlapping names/records, and resource bounds. It never
+executes a pickle. A passing synthetic preflight validates only its listed
+parser cases; the actual checkpoint remains unopened until integrator review.
+
+The preparation made no product/test edit, actual inventory execution, model load,
 inference, conversion, network request, diarization, installation, commit, or
 push. If the reader is revised, retain these first-draft bytes and the exact
 change/reason before executing any version.
